## What I analyzed

**Session `8a79f270`** — 2026-08-26, external `site-foundry` on branch `wpds-audit`, remote transport, 261 tool calls (222 Figmagent) over 201 min wall / ~70 min agent-active. Task: recreate the 11-state Build-a-Site flow on an empty Figma page from shipped React/SCSS, using real WPDS library instances and variables. Delivered 502 nodes via 76 `write`, 576 node-ops via 52 `edit`, 271 variable bindings, **zero `run_script`**.

## Three findings that mattered

**🆕 [TOOL-034] `write` can't clone more than one node per call.** `fromNodeId` is explicitly mutually exclusive with `nodes` (`create.ts:183`, `:204`), and there's no `count`. 30 of 76 writes were clones; **27 sat inside 7 consecutive runs**. ~20 calls lost. Both batch shapes are needed — same-source×N and N distinct source→parent pairs.

**🆕 [TOOL-035] `edit` can't set per-side stroke weight.** None of `strokeTopWeight`/`Bottom`/`Left`/`Right` exists anywhere in `src/`. The agent named this as its reason for **deleting three finished component variants and re-cloning them** to inherit a bottom-only card-header stroke. 8 calls where ~2 would do, plus every override re-authored. Third member of the `nodeOpSchema` field-gap family — ship with TOOL-025 and TOOL-027 in one pass.

**🔎 [BUG-016] 12th recurrence — 100% failure (5/5), worst on record.** Two of the failing nodes were built by this session minutes earlier, so no size story applies; the batch signature (`allIds`/`ids`/`dataless` all empty) recurs a 5th time, matching the v5 root cause and nothing else. Two things are new and independently actionable:
- `buildBatchExportResult` emits `OVERSIZED_FIX` only in the `dataless.length > 0` branch, so an empty-`images` batch returns **`Exported 0 node(s): none` with `isError: true` and no fix text** — a direct violation of the no-error-without-a-fix rule. Three lines, independent of the transport fix.
- The cost shape is new: the agent **didn't** defect (zero official-MCP calls, 5th consecutive session, 3rd project), so it paid in 28 read-after-write geometry checks, a `set_focus` pointing the user at the canvas, and reading the user's own hand-edits back off Figma. The 2.3% error rate looks healthy precisely *because* the agent stopped probing after minute 16.

**One escalation worth flagging:** TOOL-033's missing `height_collapse` assertion was filed as a `run_script` gap. This session used zero scripts and hit it anyway — `write` returned `"height":32` in its own response body with no warning, and the agent burned ~5 calls rediscovering it. That makes part (a) shippable alone, ahead of the harder script-node-tracking half.

No fix plans generated — none of the three new items match the Phase 6 allowlist (TOOL-034's longest run is 6, under the 20-consecutive trigger). One session remains unanalyzed (`68f20fe0`, 138 calls).
