## What the session was

`68f20fe0` — 138 calls, 45 min, external `site-foundry` on branch `wpds-audit`, remote transport. It's the **inverse of session 50**: where S50 built the Figma board from React/SCSS, this session read that board back *as the spec* to implement `BlueprintCard` and a DataViews `TemplatePicker` in code. All 30 Figmagent calls were read-only — zero `write`, `edit`, or `run_script`.

## Headline finding

**[BUG-016] and [BUG-027] are proven to be one bug** — the first behavioural demonstration, not just a code-reading inference:

The two nodes whose `read` silently returned `nodes: []` (`43:22`, `66:719`) are **the same two nodes** whose `screenshot` failed, 90 seconds apart. Both `meta` blocks were missing `nodeId`/`name`/`type` — the fingerprint of a non-object reaching the result builders from `remote/client.ts:110-114`'s `catch { return text }`.

That also **retires the "~4MB image cap" model**. The real variable is *response* size, not *image* size:

| Call | Result |
|---|---|
| `read(43:22, structure, d3)` | 40 nodes |
| `read(43:22, layout, d4)` | empty |
| `read(66:719, layout, d1)` | full COMPONENT_SET |
| `read(66:719, full, d4)` | empty |

No image is involved in either pair. Five sessions have now falsified the cap hypothesis.

## The costly part

The `screenshot` guard **asserts a cause it never measured**, and the agent obeyed it into four dead retries — `43:14` at `scale: 0.5` and `103:1135` at `format: "SVG"` each returned the *byte-identical* error. A 764×344 COMPONENT_SET failed at scale 1 while its siblings exported as SVG at 210 and 372 bytes. A wrong stated fix is worse than none, because agents act on the text.

Notably, [AGENT-001] ("stop after 2 identical errors") **doesn't fire here** — the agent changed its input each time, exactly as instructed. That gap became new entry **AGENT-029**.

## Changes made

- `figma-mcp-session51-analysis.md` — full analysis
- **BUG-016** 13th recurrence, **BUG-027** 2nd, **TOOL-022** 3rd
- **BUG-031 scope narrowed** — `read` resolved three `I…;…` instance-descendant IDs cleanly, so that defect is specific to the `run_script` VM proxy; `read`'s path is a working reference implementation for the proposed fix
- New: **AGENT-029** (prescribed-fix exhaustion), **AGENT-030** (anchored `grep` misses `Group/`-prefixed names)
- **`.claude/plans/2026-08-27-TOOL-022.md`** — the node-ID normalization, planned at its 3rd recurrence. The prior "touches multiple handlers" objection is answered by Zod `.transform()`, which leaves every handler body untouched.

`sync-issues --dry-run` parses the tracker cleanly: 100 entries, 7 creates queued, 0 drift. Manifest reports 0 sessions needing analysis. Files are left uncommitted, matching how the nightly pipeline batches its `auto-improve: session analyses` commit.

One thing worth flagging beyond the mechanics: the behavioural fix held for a **6th consecutive session across a 3rd project** — zero official-MCP defection despite a 72.7% screenshot failure rate, historically the exact trigger for it. The agent substituted structural reads to recover copy it couldn't see rendered. That's real, but it means the error count (2.3% in S50, 30% here) systematically *understates* the cost, because a well-behaved agent absorbs the gap instead of erroring on it.
